    "created_at": "2019-05-29T20:57:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-29T20:57:40Z",
    "body": "It looks like the library checks if you're online by pinging an external service (http://icanhazip.com/). The trouble with this is that this could be a pretty slow operation if DNS isn't already resolved or on high-latency connections. We could implement very short timeouts, but that may incorrectly show that you're offline on slow networks.\r\n\r\nIt would be pretty tough balancing between accuracy and speed for this kind of module. I don't know if there'd be a way to do it without a fully asynchronous prompt. 🤔 ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
